  "properties": {
    "title": "How Our Community Was Born \u2014 Looking Back on More Than 20 Years of History",
    "description": "This session will focus on the very early days of the open source geospatial community, including GRASS, UMN MapServer, the first FOSS4G conference in Bangkok, and the establishment of OSGeo.\n\nThe FOSS4G community was built through the vision, dedication, and collaboration of many pioneers of the open source geospatial movement since the 1990s.\r\n\r\nIn this keynote session, we are honored to welcome two of those pioneers\u2014Prof. Venkatesh Raghavan and Markus Neteler (joining remotely), both recipients of the Sol Katz Award\u2014to share their experiences and reflections on the formative years of our community. Together with session chair Toru Mori, who will share his own recollections of how this story began in Japan, they will look back on the emergence of projects such as GRASS GIS and UMN MapServer, the first FOSS4G conference in Bangkok in 2004, and the events that ultimately led to the establishment of the OSGeo Foundation in 2006.",
